@startuml 00-overview
!include _style.iuml
title Backend sprint 4 — the features and what links them

package "Accounts\n(01-accounts)" as Accounts {
    class loginService
    class signupService
}
package "Saved searches\n(02-saved-searches)" as Saved {
    class customSearchService
}
package "Search\n(03-search)" as Search {
    class newsService
}
package "Ingestion\n(04-ingestion)" as Ingestion {
    class ingestService
    class feedService
}
package "Sources\n(05-sources)" as Sources {
    class sourceService
    class recommendationService
}
package "Profile\n(06-profile)" as Profile {
    class profileService
}
package "Discovery\n(07-discovery)" as Discovery {
    class discoveryService
}
package "Briefing\n(08-briefing)" as Briefing {
    class briefingService
    class feedbackService
}

signupService --> profileService : creates the profile\nwith the account
profileService --> discoveryService : looks for sources\nfor the profile
profileService --> feedbackService
briefingService --> discoveryService : prunes the\nsources refused
briefingService --> feedbackService
briefingService --> ingestService
discoveryService --> sourceService
discoveryService --> ingestService : reads the\nfeeds found
discoveryService --> feedbackService
recommendationService --> feedbackService
recommendationService --> sourceService
newsService --> ingestService : Google News searches\nof the profiles
newsService --> feedService
ingestService --> feedService

note as Legend
    Every request goes router → controller → service → model → Prisma → PostgreSQL + pgvector.
    Each package has its own diagram, with its modules, their methods and the outside services.
    The shared cache (feeds, articles, stories, threads) is filled by the Ingestion in background
    and read by the Search and the Briefing.
end note
@enduml
